{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons","id":665527,"title":"About Vigor and weapons...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-15T04:53:03-07:00","id":665527,"title":"About Vigor and weapons...","content":"Something in the rulebook has caused a bit of debate between the players. Under Vigor's &quot;improved damage&quot; active effect, it says that improvised weapons take damage to their Structure when used for increased damage this way.<br /> <br /> Does this apply with normal weapons too? It would be logical that swords break and maces snap under the stress of such strength, but the book also quite clearly states that it's only a matter of improvised weaponry. What is the proper ruling here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","name":"Deraneo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:59:28-07:00","id":665656,"title":"","content":"Well, the thing is that improvised weapons already take damage when they score too many successes. Vigor just makes this worse. <br /> <br /> To think about it another way, having vigor damage <i>all</i> weapons this way would mean that a strength 1, vigor 1 vampire swinging a weapon for just one extra damage would do more damage to their weapon than a strength 10 vampire swinging without vigor would. Does that seem logical to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T08:54:38-07:00","id":665799,"title":"","content":"Personally, i don't think of it until the number of dices go above 10. That's the range of human interactuarion with tools, after all: from one/two to ten. If you go above 10, then something supernatural (or extremely exceptional) is going on. So, either way, not what you would think of normal uses for normal tools. <br /> <br /> In the case of your average fighter vampire with 3 strength, 2-3 vigor, 2-3 brawl, your knuckles won't suffer that much. But when you have that 4th Vigor point you start burning through your weapons at accelerated rate.<br /> <br /> That's the reason behind the quest after that rumored Ordo weapon infused with supernatural juice that never breaks, or those blood-forged Crone axes, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:02:06-07:00","id":665805,"title":"","content":"All weapons suffer the same stress, but normal weapons handle the stress differently. A sword used as intended will be damaged during use no matter the strength of the user (the rules always neglect this). An undamaged sword correctly used will not break no matter how much force is behind the blow. The damage to the weapon occurs because of the hardness of what it hits. You can play Solomon and have dramatic failures damage a normal weapon when Vigor is used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":".  Didn't think the point of my contrast was clear 09-15-2015, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:04:26-07:00","id":665806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=665799#post665799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, i don't think of it until the number of dices go above 10. That's the range of human interactuarion with tools, after all: from one/two to ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twelve, if we include specialities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:07:32-07:00","id":665807,"title":"","content":"I think that it says improvised weapons because they are not meant to be used as a weapon. The chair that you picked up and smashed on someone is not meant to take that kind of damage. A dagger is built to be used in combat and can handle more stress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T10:54:14-07:00","id":665893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=665806#post665806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twelve, if we include specialities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The peak mortal dice pool ignoring circumstance modifiers is well above 15.<br /> <br /> For melee combat:<br /> 5 Attribute<br /> 5 Skill<br /> 5 Stacked specialties (they cap at +5)<br /> 2 All-out-attack<br /> 3 willpower<br /> Attack: 20 Dice<br /> <br /> Now add in Light Weapon Fighting Style 2 to trade defense 1-to-1:<br /> 5 Attribute<br /> 5 Skill<br /> 5 Stacked specialties<br /> 3 Large Shield<br /> 1 Tire Iron<br /> Defense: 19 - 2 (All-out-attack can't use defense, so goes away) = +17<br /> <br /> The peak mortal dice pool in GMC as far as I can tell is 37 dice for a melee attack.<br /> <br /> Realistically though, I've rarely seen a melee specialized mortal in any of my games roll less than 10 dice before defense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":"add Willpower, All-Out, and circumstance modifiers to taste. Characters who use melee as a secondary focus tend towards 7 dice: 3 Strength, 09-15-2015, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:05:41-07:00","id":665906,"title":"","content":"Since when do stacked specialties cap at 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:09:59-07:00","id":665914,"title":"","content":"I wonder at what point a pointed piece of wood stops becoming an improvised weapon and starts becoming a stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:23:19-07:00","id":665923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=665906#post665906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when do stacked specialties cap at 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn I remembered a rule stating that bonuses from any single source capped at +/-5. Having gone back through GMC I didn't find it easily, so it might just be a house rule so common and often-referenced that I mistakenly incorporated it into my knowledge as core material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:26:24-07:00","id":665927,"title":"","content":"The question is, do specialities count as a bonus or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:33:06-07:00","id":665935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=665914#post665914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder at what point a pointed piece of wood stops becoming an improvised weapon and starts becoming a stake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say if it's carved from dense wood, sanded, and sealed its a stake. If it's broken off of a fence post or a table leg, it's improvised.<br /> <br /> So this would be improvised:<br /> <img src=\"https://littease.files.wordpress.com/2012/03/wooden-stakes.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This would be a proper stake:<br /> <img src=\"http://wiki.wodgotham.com/images/6/65/Stake.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:33:49-07:00","id":665936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=665807#post665807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it says improvised weapons because they are not meant to be used as a weapon. The chair that you picked up and smashed on someone is not meant to take that kind of damage. A dagger is built to be used in combat and can handle more stress.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the correct answer.<br /> <br /> To test for yourself, pick up the nearest chair and smash it against the wall with the force of a medium speed car crash, then see how the chair fares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:18:59-07:00","id":665962,"title":"","content":"I think most things would be seriously damaged at that speed, including professionally made swords or throwing knives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:49:45-07:00","id":665997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=665962#post665962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most things would be seriously damaged at that speed, including professionally made swords or throwing knives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Melee weapons already experience a lot of force.<br /> <br /> The whole point is that they're designed so that the flesh the weapon connects with is what takes the damage, not the weapon.<br /> <br /> If you hit something unyielding like a wall with a sword, or hit in the <i>wrong way</i>, your weapon can definitely be damaged and broken. Sounds like a perfect result for a dramatic failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:59:22-07:00","id":666009,"title":"","content":"An improvised weapon or tool is anything being used in a way or for a purpose for which it wasn't designed. Take a chair that can easily hold three hundred pounds and lay it on its side then place the same three hundred pounds on it and you end up with kindling. Take a sword that can cleave bone all day without suffering damage and use it as a pry bar, you end up with a bent or broken blade. In the case of the stake, as described it stops being an improvised weapon the moment you craft it into a true thrusting one. The same effect applies to using improvised tools, they prove inferior for the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:27:50-07:00","id":666112,"title":"","content":"The improvised weapons rules actually say to use the stats for a real weapon if it's close enough. So an improvised stake is a stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:41:11-07:00","id":666115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=666112#post666112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The improvised weapons rules actually say to use the stats for a real weapon if it's close enough. So an improvised stake is a stake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but an improvised stake would take damage with Vigor and benefit from an Improvosed Weapons Specialty while a non-improvised stake wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:36:59-07:00","id":666169,"title":"","content":"A tornado can drive a pine needle through a glass window. That would be an improvised weapon traveling around the top speed of a car. Most bullets travel faster than a car, but bullets are not damaged at all by way of the speed they travel or force applied upon them until they face an equal and opposite force applied against them or something like that. A bullet needs something as hard as bone to be deformed. Basically no matter how fast a sword is swung or thrust it won't be damaged as long as what it attempts to cut or pierce is what it was designed to damage until the blade reaches speeds at distances that would create enough friction to heat metal to the point of softening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-15-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:41:03-07:00","id":666171,"title":"","content":"I was just throwing it out there but the emphasis was meant to be on the 'at what point.' Like if you were going to make that nice shiny stake in the second picture, but another vampire burst into your haven. And you grabbed the stake, but the sealant wasn't dry, would it be improvised? What about if you hadn't put the sealant on altogether, but it was still sharpened, sanded and engraved?<br /> <br /> It was just idle wondering, nothing to be taken too seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-15-2015, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T17:54:40-07:00","id":666239,"title":"","content":"&quot;At what point&quot; is really left to ST fiat, what works best with your game at the moment. If you want the heroes to be at the disadvantage then no. Honestly even real weapons take damage with repeated use, it's just not worth worrying about in an RPG unless you want it to. It's like the old Star Wars RPG were the rules say blaster power packs only run out when the ST wants them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T18:31:46-07:00","id":666262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons?p=666171#post666171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just throwing it out there but the emphasis was meant to be on the 'at what point.' Like if you were going to make that nice shiny stake in the second picture, but another vampire burst into your haven. And you grabbed the stake, but the sealant wasn't dry, would it be improvised? What about if you hadn't put the sealant on altogether, but it was still sharpened, sanded and engraved?<br /> <br /> It was just idle wondering, nothing to be taken too seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it's mostly a question of the object's intended use. A shovel is improvised, a Shaolin spade is a weapon. A sledgehammer is improvised, a war hammer is a weapon. A random piece of wood you picked up is improvised, one you intentionally fashioned for stabbing vampires with is a weapon.<br /> <br /> Technically my definition makes some items in the weapon table improvised that aren't written as such by RAW. Crowbars, tire irons, sledgehammers, etc. But to me, if it's not made as a weapon, it should be considered improvised. YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T19:24:34-07:00","id":666312,"title":"","content":"Tools are designed to be durable as well, so I can understand them being treated as normal weapons, but under the original premise of an active use of Vigor, I think what counts as an improvised weapon can reasonably be extended beyond the usual. All weapons are designed for &quot;heavy hitting&quot; but tools are not, except sledgehammers and axes. Then it becomes a question of how much complexity a ST is willing to deal with. Regardless, this brings us beyond the original question, I think.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I watched a video of a guy try to break a sword by cutting through it with another sword. Actually he used a few different types and I think his target was a rapier. The target sword ended up bent to hell, but it didn't break. Swords don't break easily when used properly unless they are old and damaged. Wooden shafts are less forgiving, but the way the weapons are intended to be used it doesn't matter. They are just levers to transfer force to a weight. The weight takes the force that would cause the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-15-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:52:22-07:00","id":667126,"title":"","content":"Sometimes the negative aspect of an improvised weapon isn't that the weapon will break or be damaged but that it is unwieldy for that purpose. Take the crowbar for example, it's going to take a lot to bend or break a thick iron shaft but if you've ever just carried one, much less tried to swing it, you quickly realize that it isn't balanced properly for hanging onto one end and swinging. In this game I could see room to argue over how an improvised weapon works or if it will break or be damaged by that use, the rules wisely don't try to cover every possible contingency leaving it to the ST instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:38:30-07:00","id":667393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deraneo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/665527-about-vigor-and-weapons#post665527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something in the rulebook has caused a bit of debate between the players. Under Vigor's &quot;improved damage&quot; active effect, it says that improvised weapons take damage to their Structure when used for increased damage this way.<br /> <br /> Does this apply with normal weapons too? It would be logical that swords break and maces snap under the stress of such strength, but the book also quite clearly states that it's only a matter of improvised weaponry. What is the proper ruling here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well. . .as you said, the book quite clearly states that it's only a matter of improvised weaponry, so there you are! <br /> <br /> Not that you can't wing some house-rules otherwise. Just keep the following in mind if you DO decide Vigor 5 can make your sword break 1) Make sure to tell your players beforehand, 2) remember that nWoD isn't a combat simulator, so if you're trying to simulate combat more realistically be prepared for a LOT of house-rules (and probably have a lot of arguments), 3) adding in a new penalty for high vigor feels a lot like punishing a player for their character being good at something in a fairly non-creative way. There's a lot of fun ways to mess with high strength already (a character slamming a door at Strength 4 Vigor 5 can be exceptionally amusing, as can dramatic failures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T16:59:26-07:00","id":683643,"title":"","content":"So how exactly does this work if you try to beat someone with someone else? Conscious or otherwise. Do you still do the durability thing? Do people even have a durability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T00:24:44-07:00","id":684006,"title":"","content":"It's easiest if they're wearing armour. Otherwise you could use stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}